{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Multiplicity"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.laurentTwoVal_one_add_qinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.laurentTwoVal_one_add_qinv","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/LaurentTwoValuation.lean#L90-L103","doc":"**`v_[2](1+q⁻¹) = 1`** — the single `[2]_q` factor of `1+q⁻¹ = q⁻¹·(q+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.one_add_qinv_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.one_add_qinv_eq","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/LaurentTwoValuation.lean#L84-L88","doc":"`1 + q⁻¹ = q⁻¹·(q+1)` — the odd-branch image of `q⁻¹` in the fundamental\ncycle, exhibiting the single `[2]_q` factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.laurentTwoVal_qinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.laurentTwoVal_qinv","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/LaurentTwoValuation.lean#L76-L82","doc":"**`v_[2](q⁻¹) = 0`** — `q⁻¹ = T(-1)` is a unit, with no `[2]_q` factor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.laurentTwoVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.laurentTwoVal","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/LaurentTwoValuation.lean#L72-L74","doc":"The **`[2]_q`-adic valuation** on `ℤ[q^{±1}]`: the `(q+1)`-adic multiplicity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.not_T1_add_one_dvd_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.not_T1_add_one_dvd_T","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/LaurentTwoValuation.lean#L65-L68","doc":"`[2]_q` does not divide a unit — in particular not `T n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.T1_add_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.T1_add_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/LaurentTwoValuation.lean#L58-L63","doc":"**`[2]_q = q+1 ≠ 0`** in `ℤ[q^{±1}]` (its value at `q = 1` is `2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.T1_add_one_not_isUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.T1_add_one_not_isUnit","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/LaurentTwoValuation.lean#L51-L56","doc":"**`[2]_q = q+1` is not a unit in `ℤ[q^{±1}]`** — it vanishes at `q = -1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.evalOne_T1_add_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.evalOne_T1_add_one","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/LaurentTwoValuation.lean#L46-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.evalNegOne_T1_add_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.evalNegOne_T1_add_one","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/LaurentTwoValuation.lean#L41-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.evalOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.evalOne","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/LaurentTwoValuation.lean#L37-L39","doc":"**Evaluation at `q = 1`** as a ring hom `ℤ[q^{±1}] → ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.evalNegOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.LaurentTwoValuation.evalNegOne","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/LaurentTwoValuation.lean#L32-L35","doc":"**Evaluation at `q = -1`** as a ring hom `ℤ[q^{±1}] → ℤ` (`-1` is a unit in\n`ℤ`, so `T ↦ -1` extends over the Laurent ring). ","signatureChunk":0}]}